{
  "_comment": "Template for per-repo .claude/settings.json on Phase 2 dev-team targets. push-to-repos.sh installs this. Strip _comment fields when applying.",
  "_comment_promptSuggestionEnabled": "OFF in dev-team repos as a SAFETY control, not a preference. Claude Code renders its generated composer suggestion in the same input cells as typed text, distinguished only by colour \u2014 and the window-content API every watcher here reads (Terminal 'get contents') strips colour. A suggestion is therefore byte-identical to a human's typed-but-unsubmitted draft, so any automation that submits 'stranded input' can feed a session its own advice under the CEO's authority (observed 2026-08-27; two attempts). /handoff also exports CLAUDE_CODE_ENABLE_PROMPT_SUGGESTION=0 at launch, which takes precedence; this key covers sessions started by hand in the repo, which the launch env does not reach. See docs/memos/2026-08-27-rca-observed-text-is-not-attributed-text.md.",
  "promptSuggestionEnabled": false,
  "_comment_permissions": "PERMISSIONS POSTURE (CEO 2026-11-01): lenient harness, the sprint brief is the gate. Blanket Bash so a lane never stalls on routine work; ask carries only the never-uninvited set — force-push, remote branch deletion, PR merge (lanes never merge; land-lane does, from the CTO home), launchd persistence, GitHub repo create/delete, edits to its own permission files. An ask rule beats any allow rule, so each prompts every time; an unattended lane that hits one stalls visibly (IDLE in /sprint-status) rather than acting. Project additions go in <cto-home>/.cto/settings-overlay.json (merged by push-to-repos.sh).",
  "permissions": {
    "allow": [
      "Bash",
      "Edit",
      "Write",
      "Read",
      "Glob",
      "Grep",
      "WebFetch",
      "WebSearch",
      "mcp__domshell__domshell_execute"
    ],
    "ask": [
      "Bash(git push --force*)",
      "Bash(git push -f *)",
      "Bash(git push * --force*)",
      "Bash(git push * -f *)",
      "Bash(git push --delete *)",
      "Bash(git push * --delete *)",
      "Bash(git push * -d *)",
      "Bash(gh pr merge *)",
      "Bash(launchctl load *)",
      "Bash(launchctl unload *)",
      "Bash(launchctl bootstrap *)",
      "Bash(launchctl bootout *)",
      "Bash(gh repo create *)",
      "Bash(gh repo delete *)",
      "Bash(gh repo edit *)",
      "Edit(.claude/settings.json)",
      "Edit(.claude/settings.local.json)",
      "Write(.claude/settings.json)",
      "Write(.claude/settings.local.json)"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "_comment_SessionStart": "inject-devteam-contract: loads CLAUDE.devteam.md as context in upstream/public clones where the tracked CLAUDE.md belongs to the upstream project (inert everywhere else). auto-paste-brief: pastes .claude/pending-prompt.md into context and records session_id for /peek and /resume-dev-team. inject-project-layer: prints the project's and this repo's standing orders (CEO 2026-11-04; scripts/agentic/project-layer.sh).",
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/inject-devteam-contract.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/auto-paste-brief.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/inject-project-layer.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "_comment_SessionEnd": "Record session end + touch .claude/CRASHED on unclean exit so the CTO's /sprint-status sees it.",
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/session-end-record.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "_comment_Stop": "On every turn end: check-complete touches .claude/COMPLETE when dev-report.md lands (so /sprint-status sees it); derived-artifact-reminder runs the ADR-002 gate in audit mode and tells the session ONCE per new finding that a governed derived artifact is stale (inert unless .claude/derived-artifacts.yaml exists).",
    "Stop": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/check-complete.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/derived-artifact-reminder.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "_comment_PreToolUse": "Two path/lane guards. deny-self-commit: the CTO commits after the independent Phase-3 review; a session that can close its own gate collapses the separation the sprint lifecycle depends on. deny-generated-edit: generated artifacts change through their generator, never by hand \u2014 INERT unless the repo declares globs in .claude/generated-paths. deny-authorization-forge: a dev lane does not write CEO-AUTHORIZATION.md \u2014 the CTO records the CEO's words from the conversation (CEO ruling 2026-10-30).",
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/deny-self-commit.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/deny-authorization-forge.sh"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/deny-generated-edit.sh"
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/deny-authorization-forge.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
